First, create a function that takes the GRanges object and the subset argument as inputs. Within this function, you can use an if statement to check the subset argument and subset the GRanges accordingly. For example, if the subset argument is "start", you can subset the GRanges based on the start position of the ranges.

Next, use the subset() function from the GenomicRanges package to filter the GRanges object based on the specified criteria. For example, if you want to subset the GRanges based on the start position being less than a certain value, you can use the following code:
```R
subset_granges <- function(gr, subset_arg) {
  if(subset_arg == "start") {
    subset_granges <- subset(gr, start(gr) < 100)
  }
  return(subset_granges)
}
